From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: Offer NV12 and decode to system memory on macOS.

The base skips MFVideoFormat_NV12 in the video decoder's
GetOutputAvailableType on macOS (CrossOver hack 26265). Windows and
WineHQ list NV12 first. A player that accepts only NV12, such as Unreal
Engine's Electra media player, finds no usable output type and tears
the decoder down: observed on macOS, its videos stay black and a
cutscene never finishes.

Offering NV12 alone is not enough on macOS. The decoder advertises
MF_SA_D3D_AWARE and MF_SA_D3D11_AWARE, so such a player hands it a D3D
device manager and asks for DXGI surface output. mfplat then fails to
create the NV12 staging texture it reads that output back through
(E_INVALIDARG), because the macOS D3D11 implementations do not support
it, and ProcessOutput fails with MF_E_UNEXPECTED.

Remove the skip and, on macOS, report both attributes as FALSE so the
H.264, WMV and IV50 decoders write to system memory, unlike Windows
and WineHQ. Nothing is keyed on a program and nothing is configurable.

---
diff --git a/dlls/winegstreamer/video_decoder.c b/dlls/winegstreamer/video_decoder.c
index 0c40c29..0564b58 100644
--- a/dlls/winegstreamer/video_decoder.c
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/video_decoder.c
@@ -605,16 +605,6 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI transform_GetOutputAvailableType(IMFTransform *iface, DWOR
     if (index >= decoder->output_type_count)
         return MF_E_NO_MORE_TYPES;
 
-    /* CW HACK 26265 */
-    if (is_macos() && IsEqualGUID(decoder->output_types[index], &MFVideoFormat_NV12))
-    {
-        WARN("Skipping NV12 output format\n");
-        index++;
-
-        if (index >= decoder->output_type_count)
-            return MF_E_NO_MORE_TYPES;
-    }
-
     return create_output_media_type(decoder, decoder->output_types[index], NULL, type);
 }
 
@@ -1676,9 +1666,12 @@ static HRESULT video_decoder_create_with_types(const GUID *const *input_types, U
         goto failed;
     if (FAILED(hr = MFCreateAttributes(&decoder->attributes, 16)))
         goto failed;
+    /* The macOS D3D11 implementations cannot create the NV12 staging texture
+     * mfplat needs to read back DXGI surface output, so decode to system
+     * memory there instead of advertising D3D awareness. */
     if (FAILED(hr = IMFAttributes_SetUINT32(decoder->attributes, &MF_LOW_LATENCY, FALSE))
-            || FAILED(hr = IMFAttributes_SetUINT32(decoder->attributes, &MF_SA_D3D_AWARE, TRUE))
-            || FAILED(hr = IMFAttributes_SetUINT32(decoder->attributes, &MF_SA_D3D11_AWARE, TRUE))
+            || FAILED(hr = IMFAttributes_SetUINT32(decoder->attributes, &MF_SA_D3D_AWARE, !is_macos()))
+            || FAILED(hr = IMFAttributes_SetUINT32(decoder->attributes, &MF_SA_D3D11_AWARE, !is_macos()))
             || FAILED(hr = IMFAttributes_SetUINT32(decoder->attributes,
                     &MFT_DECODER_EXPOSE_OUTPUT_TYPES_IN_NATIVE_ORDER, FALSE)))
         goto failed;
